# Print is physical

Someone prints these files and cuts material to them. A 2 mm error costs money.

- Real units only (mm/cm) in the print DOM. Dual-DOM is mandatory: screen
  version scaled in px, print version in real units.
- One px↔mm constant, from src/print/. Never redefine locally.
- Never mark a print criterion done on screen evidence. It requires a measured,
  photographed printout.
- Print gaps route back to the print engine. Never patch print CSS inside a
  feature folder.

Per-output page/margin/unit values are frozen in PRINT_CONTRACT.md. Do not
infer them from legacy files — the contract is authoritative and some legacy
values were wrong (the carton template prints px-only with no mm conversion).
